141:### US-03-R1-F02 — `persist()` skips the write instead of clearing (minor)
142-
143-`quote-store.ts:169`: `if (plan === null && Object.keys(this.valuesSignal()).length === 0) return;`
144-
145-- The goal of a3f186c (an empty state leaves no entry) is reasonable. ADR-0003 does not require an
146-  entry before the first value, and every US-01 unit and e2e test still passes (945/945, 124/124).
147-  But the guard returns, it doesn't remove, so the invariant "empty state ⇒ no entry" holds only
148-  when storage was already empty. In `prune()` (`:88-98`), if every stored key is no longer
149-  configured, `valuesSignal` becomes `{}` and nothing is written. The previous entry, with the
150-  values of the removed fields (possibly personal data), stays in the tab until the person types
151-  again. ADR-0003 says "The pruned state is written back." The UI doesn't show the stale values
152-  (they are pruned again on every load), so the impact is small. That's why this is minor.
153-- The commit came from test assertions that go further than the spec. US-03-AC-11 requires "no
154-  `quote-wizard` entry" only *on the confirmation*; for reload, back and "Nueva cotización" it
155-  requires empty fields and no plan. The e2e tests (`us-01-03-full-flow-co.spec.ts:564,575`) and
156-  the d530005 unit test also require `null` storage on step 1. That stricter reading is defensible
157-  (data minimisation), but it changes US-01 behaviour (entering a country used to write
158-  `{country, values: {}}`) and should be recorded.
159-- **Direction:** replace the `return` with `clearStorage()` (then return), so the invariant holds
160-  in every case. Record it as an **ADR-0003 implementation note** in `adr/README.md` ("an empty
161-  wizard state is represented by no entry; entering a country writes nothing until the first
162-  value"). Later stories read ADR-0003 to learn when the entry exists, so the note is needed.
